ue "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339828} :answer-field/id #uuid "7df87fa2-2bdf-5af2-bcd5-28691af80256" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341601}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f7492471-0301-5306-8f40-5431247eb08f" :question/math-academy-id "q-73743" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390388 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9973610-47f9-5f62-a4ae-54d727ff19bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1-2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390390} {:answer/id #uuid "c2ddc9c8-cf3c-5347-a18e-5fc3f7cd82d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2-4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390391} {:answer/id #uuid "4142878a-1989-59e7-bb13-e08f2f47a895" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2-4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390392} {:answer/id #uuid "15cec20b-2ee9-50b2-83e8-5d388cb51a75" 