$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266071 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27acee71-ab8c-52c4-b380-e4b7372ca488" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st, $2$nd, and $5$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263345} {:answer/id #uuid "2e94901f-f7d7-5cff-b060-2a6bc9fe13d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263392} {:answer/id #uuid "9ea9a68a-c47d-5e85-9972-485e74023990" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st and $3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264352} {:answer/id #uuid "b99614d4-5b37-532d-9966-4aa4c25ae913" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st, $3$rd, and $5$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264607} {:answer/id #uuid "d2e2c029-4762-5ffd-9154-e522d95553de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b99614d4-5b37-532d-9966-4aa4c25ae913" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st, $3$rd, and $5$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264607} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a9fb951-1e52-5b4b-ab1b-fc828771accf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265386}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b653b8c3-f330-53fd-9729-fc5cdad2a545" :question/math-academy-id "q-131305" :question/problem "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $P,$ given by\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $P$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $P$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $3$rd, and $5$th columns."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266072 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34058259-6e2b-5f85-a03a-e2f9d0c05ea5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263454} {:answer/id #uuid "637ae12f-f047-5ccb-923f-26c35358f048" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st, $3$rd, and $5$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263860} {:answer/id #uuid "a863b2f6-a56d-59c1-a785-24d6aaf11f39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st, $2$nd, $3$rd, and $5$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264438} {:answer/id #uuid "eed33b0c-85e3-5720-bdce-154c2d9de501" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st, $3$rd, $4$th, and $5$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265091} {:answer/id #uuid "f1919136-3117-5c54-a549-436efa2ab932" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st, $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265122}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a863b2f6-a56d-59c1-a785-24d6aaf11f39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st, $2$nd, $3$rd, and $5$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264438} :answer-field/id #uuid "51f840dd-2ff6-5f06-b2ec-3c22674a0dd5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265394}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ccd071ca-5d5f-5313-be82-604c8c6af243" :question/math-academy