on "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $2$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402461 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e2cc6e3-e6bd-532d-8f1f-9b390c501b74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st and $2$nd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402463} {:answer/id #uuid "6fdb0769-e31b-5103-99f8-7c1edc831761" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402464} {:answer/id #uuid "a11b1eb4-e2a7-524e-a084-458df3eaa259" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd and $3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402465} {:answer/id #uuid "fc893d60-072c-5dca-bf01-c98cdfe541a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$rd and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402466} {:answer/id #uuid "697bc745-dc44-59f7-92ec-a23865a1d921" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "697bc745-dc44-59f7-92ec-a23865a1d921" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402467} :answer-field/id #uuid "b29827dc-7c2e-5a8a-9cf8-9120c56fe561" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402462}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7d0368b2-c48d-55b9-a038-5636deca9c98" :question/math-academy-id "q-35757" :question/problem "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th columns."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403682 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62c7b061-ae07-587c-bab0-15049cf99b56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403684} {:answer/id #uuid "bc30072d-7cf1-5da5-97b9-253a92f7877b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$nd and $3$rd only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403685} {:answer/id #uuid "508efe11-c663-52c3-84b8-ac714fe99937" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403686} {:answer/id #uuid "8054e257-e2ab-5aa6-b464-152bde3bafb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st, $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403687} {:answer/id #uuid "56527d12-3319-58cd-8ff8-f8efdf4d8acf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403688}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8054e257-e2ab-5aa6-b464-152bde3bafb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$st, $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403687} :answer-field/id #uuid "6197e392-74ff-5689-be7c-741e44610b04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403683}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8bbb774c-4bbb-58f8-84cb-fd20b0029b02" :question/math-academy-id "q-73638" :question/problem "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $P,$ given by\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $P$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & ↔{R}_{4} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $P$ has $4$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th columns."}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix"}]}
